From fd80e034ce68b2566cedd59eb15c98426b6cbce9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:12:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] Bluetooth: MGMT: Free pending mesh sends when the
 controller is removed

A Mesh Send is queued on hdev->mesh_pending when another transmission
is on air, and is started when that one is done. Only the transmission
whose start is queued is freed at unregister, by hci_cmd_sync_clear().
The requests behind it stay on the list: mgmt_index_removed() cancels
the delayed work that would have started them, and nothing frees them.
mgmt_cleanup() frees the requests of a socket when it is closed, but it
walks hci_dev_list, which no longer holds the controller by then. Each
request holds a reference on its mgmt socket, so the socket is pinned
too, and neither Mesh Packet Complete nor anything else is ever sent
for them. Both the requests and the sockets are reported by kmemleak
once the freed hci_dev is out of the way.

Free the pending requests in mgmt_index_removed(), after the delayed
work is cancelled and with hdev->lock held, as its caller holds it. They
are completed silently, as mgmt_cleanup() does for a closing socket;
the Index Removed event has been sent.
---
 net/bluetooth/mgmt.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index 922bc28bc1c67..a5a8b4592c6df 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -9935,6 +9935,7 @@ void mgmt_index_removed(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
 	struct mgmt_ev_ext_index ev;
 	struct cmd_lookup match = { NULL, hdev, MGMT_STATUS_INVALID_INDEX };
+	struct mgmt_mesh_tx *mesh_tx;
 
 	if (hci_test_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_RAW_DEVICE))
 		return;
@@ -9963,6 +9964,14 @@ void mgmt_index_removed(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&hdev->service_cache);
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&hdev->rpa_expired);
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&hdev->mesh_send_done);
+
+	/* Nothing will start or complete the Mesh Send requests that are still
+	 * pending, and mgmt_cleanup() will not find this controller any more
+	 * when their socket is closed. Free them now: each one holds a
+	 * reference on its socket.
+	 */
+	while ((mesh_tx = mgmt_mesh_next(hdev, NULL)))
+		mesh_send_complete(hdev, mesh_tx, true);
 }
 
 void mgmt_power_on(struct hci_dev *hdev, int err)
